{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1490273-if-disciplines-were-to-give-passive-bonuses","id":1490273,"title":"If Disciplines Were to Give Passive Bonuses","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-15T10:59:19-07:00","id":1490273,"title":"If Disciplines Were to Give Passive Bonuses","content":"<span style=\"font-size:15px\">Doing some theory game crafting. If disciplines gave passive skill bonuses ala Awe or Daunt, which would give what do you think?<br /> Obfuscation: Stealth<br /> Auspex: Awareness<br /> Animalism: Animal Handling<br /> etc.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":490,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","user":"omenseer","date":". 08-15-2022, 02:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-15T11:43:01-07:00","id":1490276,"title":"","content":"I have taken it a step further in some of my own theory crafting by giving pros and cons in the form of permanent upgrades.<br /> <br /> For example, taking Fortitude deadens the nerves, so you can't feel as much, but this means you can also do all the vampire scenes where something that hurts a lot isn't as big a deal. Likewise, Auspex is very powerful, usually either passive or at least blood cost free, so your enhanced senses are always on, thus bright lights, strong smells, loud sounds are overwhelming to you. If you take both Fortitude and Auspex, the negatives cancel each other out.<br /> <br /> Obfuscate is great for hiding, but how do you handle the character if Obfuscate makes you forgettable, in the same way as the Sidereal exalted are constantly being forgotten. Presence makes others pay attention to you and eventually worship you, but what happens when that makes stealth close to impossible because everyone always looks your way. Once again, by purchasing or taking both disciplines, the negatives cancel.<br /> <br /> This brings some of the classical vampire weaknesses back into the game, but at the same time makes the character growth feel meaningful as they stack pros and cons on the character.<br /> <br /> I get what you are trying to do with the Discipline giving back to the base stats, but V:tM seems to want the disciplines to be an extension of the stats, hence why you often have to spec into those stats heavily to get functional use out of said power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-15T23:41:26-07:00","id":1490353,"title":"","content":"Common Disciplines are largely passive/have their own passive traits? The physicals speak for themselves, though celerity transitioned to passive status recently.. Just having animalism improves how animals treat you. Obfuscate and Dominate are incredibly easy to use and are more of a checkbox than something the vampire needs to think about . Hieghtened senses is another checkbox and Auspex provides premonitions. Protean's first power is another free to use checkbox. It's really just Presence (and celerity, depending on edition) that doesn't offer passives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T02:33:45-07:00","id":1490360,"title":"","content":"I have considered this too, either as a passive effect for each Discipline or as a part of their first Discipline dot. <br /> <br /> But then I feel it should be limited to mundane actions -- so you don't get the Presence bonus to other Presence actions; only to actions where you're using otherwise mundane skill. <br /> <br /> Then it becomes more of a passive/active split, like the physical Disciplines in V20. You get either one; not both. You'd then need to add specific powers, or more and better active uses, to the physical Disciplines so they're not underpowered.<br /> <br /> If I were to key them to Abilities, they would add to the following:<br /> Animalism: Animal Ken<br /> Auspex: Alertness, Awareness or Investigation when using any of the senses<br /> Daimonion: Empathy or Subterfuge when identifying or exploiting others' sins<br /> Dementation: Intimidation or Subterfuge when trying to inflame madness<br /> Dominate: Intimidation or Leadership when commanding others <br /> Melpominee: Expression or Performance when using the voice<br /> Mytherceria: Academics or Occult for creating or deciphering riddles, enigmas and faerie magic <br /> Necromancy: N/A<br /> Obfuscate: Stealth<br /> Presence: Expression or Subterfuge when influencing others <br /> Protean: Survival when hunting or enduring environmental extremes<br /> Quietus: Athletics or Medicine when using vitae<br /> Thaumaturgy: N/A<br /> Vicissitude: Stealth or Performance when disguising oneself<br /> Visceratika: Athletics when flying or Stealth when among stone, brick and concrete<br /> <br /> But as you can see, it doesn't quite fit neatly, as there are too many overlaps, so it ends up becoming 'x Ability when y applies'.<br /> <br /> You'd also have to check which Abilities are used for which Discipline powers, as there probably should be some synergy there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T03:43:27-07:00","id":1490363,"title":"","content":"Maybe each Discipline is linked to either a specific Ability, or two specific Ability specialties. If you have any dots in that Discipline you can spend a bloodpoint to reduce the difficulty of all rolls related to that Discpline's Ability/Specialty by 1. I generally wouldn't do much more than that though. A small semi-passive bonus but nothing too much. Most Disciplines already give cool shit, and vampires can boost their Attributes with blood anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}